  "notes": "v323 — TIMER-REANCHORED-MIDDAY + LOADS-DOUBLE-COUNTING (owner's live Nov 4, 2026 Aecon day: the tracker paused itself mid-day and showed ~3h41m for a full paid day; load counting missed cycles in the morning, then counted twice). (1) sessionFacts now sends the segment BASE as the record's elapsedBase — the native record adds the live segment itself, so sending the total made the record (widget/PiP faces) count the segment TWICE (harness-proven: record read 21600 s at a true 10800 s; a native pause froze an inflated 24038 s for a true 13238 s and adoption imported it wholesale). (2) adoptSessionRecord clamps any adopted total to the session's own wall-clock age, so a legacy inflated record can never push the day past its start. (3) The peg fence-recovery is symmetric: it now serves the LOAD side while the cycle waits to arm (v300 served only the dump side) — a pickup face that moved outside the load fence no longer starves the arm all day (his morning cycles 2-3). (4) Hand-tap race closed: a +1 tapped at the tip while the machine is carrying marks the carry hand-counted; if the machine then confirms that same tip, the correction retires as the count lands — one physical load reads once (his afternoon doubles). Two movement-shaped limits are documented in the suite, not gated (an empty full-dwell cycle-shape, a full-dwell queue creep across a close pair — GPS-indistinguishable from real cycles under the generous-fence law). Proof: tools/defects-nov4-v323-test.js 20/20; v282/v284/v300 peg + recovery suites and the v265/v271/v303/v314 session suites all still green. Reaches his phone on next full app close + reopen. Verdict owed in his hands.",
